00:20:44.014 --> 00:20:46.683
Since I bought this robot for Jun,

00:20:46.767 --> 00:20:49.686
can you buy me a bowl of jjajangmyeon?

00:20:52.606 --> 00:20:55.817
This is a family park the company
has been running for over 20 years

00:20:55.901 --> 00:20:58.028
as part of its corporate
social responsibility initiative.

00:20:58.612 --> 00:21:00.781
There's a playground for the kids
over there.

00:21:00.864 --> 00:21:04.076
We also built a fountain plaza
and a nature learning center

00:21:04.159 --> 00:21:06.078
to make it a fun and relaxing
family-friendly park.

00:21:06.745 --> 00:21:09.664
It's huge. This place is so nice.

00:21:09.748 --> 00:21:12.042
I know, and even the admission is free.

00:21:12.125 --> 00:21:14.336
How did I not know about this place?

00:21:14.419 --> 00:21:16.004
But I don't see many visitors.

00:21:16.755 --> 00:21:20.300
As of late,
corporate support has been minimal.

00:21:20.384 --> 00:21:23.053
That's why promotion is limited
and the facilities are showing their age,

00:21:23.136 --> 00:21:25.847
which has led to a steady decline
in visitors.

00:21:25.931 --> 00:21:28.183
Then why did they build it
in the first place?

00:21:30.894 --> 00:21:32.396
So, what are we here to do today?

00:21:37.901 --> 00:21:39.111
My back is killing me.

00:21:39.194 --> 00:21:41.446
Are we being punished
for screwing up the livestream?

00:21:41.530 --> 00:21:43.323
It hasn't even been a month
since I got my laser treatment.

00:21:43.407 --> 00:21:44.533
What if it all goes to waste?

00:21:45.659 --> 00:21:47.828
We should be thankful
we still have our jobs.

00:21:47.911 --> 00:21:49.871
This is nothing compared to giving birth.

00:21:49.955 --> 00:21:51.748
Yeah, you're totally right about that.

00:21:51.832 --> 00:21:54.292
I passed out
when I was giving birth to my oldest.

00:21:54.376 --> 00:21:56.628
I was in labor for 12 hours,

00:21:56.711 --> 00:21:59.548
and my kid's head got stuck in my pelvis
because it was so big.

00:22:00.132 --> 00:22:02.175
They had no choice
but to use a vacuum extractor,

00:22:02.259 --> 00:22:04.136
and my kid's head is still dented.

00:22:04.219 --> 00:22:06.847
I cried so much
about my kid having a cone-head.

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:08.515
I don't even remember the pain.

00:22:08.598 --> 00:22:10.934
What about you, Da-rim?
How was it for you?

00:22:11.518 --> 00:22:12.352
What?

00:22:14.604 --> 00:22:15.981
For me…

00:22:17.232 --> 00:22:18.567
What was it again?

00:22:18.650 --> 00:22:20.694
What did Mom say about my birth again?

00:22:22.112 --> 00:22:24.406
I was in labor for a full day and a half,

00:22:24.489 --> 00:22:26.867
but in the end,
they had to do a C-section--

00:22:29.161 --> 00:22:31.454
-What's wrong?
-You poor thing.

00:22:31.538 --> 00:22:34.082
Jun better be
the world's greatest son to you.

00:22:34.166 --> 00:22:36.209
-What?
-That's the greatest injustice.

00:22:36.293 --> 00:22:38.628
You go through all that labor pain
just to have surgery.

00:22:38.712 --> 00:22:40.172
But isn't it just amazing?

00:22:40.255 --> 00:22:43.800
As soon as you see your baby,
you forget all about the pain.

00:22:43.884 --> 00:22:44.885
I know, right?

00:22:44.968 --> 00:22:47.345
You're so right.

00:22:47.429 --> 00:22:51.308
He was so adorable with such fair skin.
I thought I gave birth to an angel.

00:22:51.391 --> 00:22:53.101
Your newborn was adorable with fair skin?

00:22:53.185 --> 00:22:55.478
They're all red and wrinkly.

00:22:56.730 --> 00:23:00.400
You know, it sometimes sounds like
you've never raised a child.

00:23:01.026 --> 00:23:02.194
-What?
-Da-rim.

00:23:02.777 --> 00:23:04.487
There was also that diaper incident.

00:23:06.072 --> 00:23:07.574
You've never raised a kid, have you?

00:23:11.203 --> 00:23:13.121
What are you talking about?

00:23:13.205 --> 00:23:14.998
I fed and bathed him myself.

00:23:15.081 --> 00:23:16.958
Don't lie to us. We can just tell.

00:23:17.042 --> 00:23:18.627
Your hands look like
they've never done hard work.

00:23:18.710 --> 00:23:21.129
Just look at that soft and smooth skin.

00:23:27.219 --> 00:23:28.345
Oh no.

00:23:29.012 --> 00:23:30.555
Have I been exposed?

00:23:31.097 --> 00:23:34.893
I bet her loving husband
changed every diaper

00:23:34.976 --> 00:23:38.855
and made sure
she didn't even lift a finger.

00:23:38.939 --> 00:23:40.148
And the baby

00:23:40.232 --> 00:23:43.443
probably takes after his handsome father.

00:23:43.526 --> 00:23:46.154
That's probably why she thought
he looked like an angel.

00:23:46.238 --> 00:23:48.740
-You know how it goes.
-Loving husband, my ass.

00:23:48.823 --> 00:23:52.577
-I should get out of here.
-Of course, her husband is so handsome.

00:23:52.661 --> 00:23:54.788
-My back is killing me.
-I'd like to see his handsome face.

00:23:54.871 --> 00:23:55.789
I'm telling you, Nan-suk.

00:23:55.872 --> 00:23:58.083
-He's ridiculously handsome.
-Really?

00:23:58.166 --> 00:24:02.128
-Yeah, he is.
-Goodness gracious.

00:24:02.212 --> 00:24:03.797
How can someone be so lucky?

00:24:03.880 --> 00:24:06.633
And she gave birth to a son. How perfect.

00:24:08.343 --> 00:24:09.678
That was a close call.

00:24:10.345 --> 00:24:12.305
I should just shut up if I don't know.

00:24:20.313 --> 00:24:22.607
Do you want some help?

00:24:22.691 --> 00:24:23.984
Really?

00:24:24.067 --> 00:24:25.277
-Thank you so much.
-Not at all.

00:24:27.279 --> 00:24:29.239
You must've been uncomfortable.

00:24:29.823 --> 00:24:31.658
Just hold on a second.

00:24:32.242 --> 00:24:33.535
Here we go.

00:24:33.618 --> 00:24:34.452
That's it.

00:24:34.536 --> 00:24:35.787
You're so cute.

00:24:36.496 --> 00:24:38.498
-All done.
-Oh gosh.

00:24:39.833 --> 00:24:41.501
-Thank you.
-It was nothing.

00:24:41.584 --> 00:24:43.545
I actually hurt my hand.

00:24:43.628 --> 00:24:45.422
You're really good at this.

00:24:45.505 --> 00:24:48.633
I practiced a lot while watching videos.

00:24:49.926 --> 00:24:52.554
But I noticed you were using
a foreign brand of diapers.

00:24:53.221 --> 00:24:56.599
A Korean brand called Natural BeBe
also sells excellent diapers.

00:24:57.934 --> 00:25:01.271
I know, but this brand donates
part of its proceeds

00:25:01.354 --> 00:25:02.897
to environmental protection.

00:25:03.398 --> 00:25:06.109
The environment has become
my biggest concern after giving birth.

00:25:06.693 --> 00:25:09.612
When you realize that this world is
where your child will grow up and live in,

00:25:10.196 --> 00:25:11.990
your mindset shifts.

00:25:12.490 --> 00:25:13.825
I see.

00:25:14.492 --> 00:25:16.661
Seeing myself change like this

00:25:18.580 --> 00:25:19.914
makes me realize that motherhood

00:25:20.749 --> 00:25:22.125
is pretty amazing.

00:25:58.620 --> 00:26:01.081
It's just as cool as the Grandfather Tree
in my neighborhood.

00:26:15.804 --> 00:26:16.638
What's that?

00:26:18.181 --> 00:26:19.391
"Gong Ji-hyeok"?

00:26:21.101 --> 00:26:21.935
Wait.

00:26:24.646 --> 00:26:25.480
What are you doing?

00:26:26.898 --> 00:26:29.776
Mr. Gong, your name is here.

00:26:29.859 --> 00:26:31.111
"Gong Ji-hyeok Tree."

00:26:35.657 --> 00:26:37.992
GONG JI-HYEOK TREE
APRIL 5, 2002

00:26:49.212 --> 00:26:50.088
Here we go.

00:26:54.759 --> 00:26:55.593
All done.

00:26:57.971 --> 00:27:00.932
GONG JI-HYEOK TREE
APRIL 5, 2002

00:27:01.015 --> 00:27:02.100
Okay.

00:27:02.183 --> 00:27:03.601
Look over here.

00:27:05.103 --> 00:27:07.605
One, two, three.

00:27:10.775 --> 00:27:12.694
So it's a tree you planted
with your mother.

00:27:13.736 --> 00:27:14.904
It must bring back memories.

00:27:15.655 --> 00:27:17.615
I just planted it
and never took care of it,

00:27:17.699 --> 00:27:19.617
but it grew up strong all on its own.

00:27:20.785 --> 00:27:22.745
You should
bring your mother here sometime.

00:27:25.457 --> 00:27:26.332
I'm not sure

00:27:27.000 --> 00:27:28.168
if that'll be possible.

00:27:30.044 --> 00:27:31.838
She's at the same hospital as your mother.

00:27:32.839 --> 00:27:34.257
She's been unwell for a long time.

00:27:36.468 --> 00:27:39.471
So that's why we ran into each other
at the hospital last time.

00:27:40.805 --> 00:27:42.640
It must've been tough for you as well.

00:27:43.391 --> 00:27:45.727
I hope she gets better soon.

00:27:50.607 --> 00:27:52.901
Oh, then how about
I take a picture of you with it

00:27:52.984 --> 00:27:54.235
so you can show it to your mother?

00:27:54.319 --> 00:27:55.945
I'm sure she'll love it.

00:27:56.029 --> 00:27:57.280
Stand there.

00:27:57.363 --> 00:27:58.531
I'll take the picture.

00:28:00.325 --> 00:28:01.701
Stand right there.

00:28:02.285 --> 00:28:03.578
That looks good.

00:28:05.330 --> 00:28:06.623
Maybe you should pose.

00:28:09.709 --> 00:28:11.794
That's great,

00:28:11.878 --> 00:28:14.214
but how about we go for something cute?

00:28:14.297 --> 00:28:15.173
Cute?

00:28:15.256 --> 00:28:16.174
Yes, cute.

00:28:19.761 --> 00:28:21.221
That's pretty cute,

00:28:21.804 --> 00:28:22.931
but maybe add a cheek heart?

00:28:23.014 --> 00:28:25.099
Or an ear heart,

00:28:25.183 --> 00:28:26.684
a bear heart, or a cat heart.

00:28:26.768 --> 00:28:28.311
Or maybe a giant one like this.

00:28:29.604 --> 00:28:31.606
Stop laughing and do it.

00:28:31.689 --> 00:28:32.982
Your mom will love it.

00:28:35.735 --> 00:28:36.778
Here we go.

00:28:36.861 --> 00:28:38.112
Get ready.

00:28:38.196 --> 00:28:40.198
He really is very handsome.

00:28:40.281 --> 00:28:41.449
Oh, right.

00:28:41.533 --> 00:28:42.575
Are you ready?

00:28:42.659 --> 00:28:43.993
One, two, three.

00:28:44.077 --> 00:28:45.620
So cute.

00:28:45.703 --> 00:28:47.455
Next. One, two, three.

00:28:48.248 --> 00:28:49.082
Great.

00:28:49.165 --> 00:28:50.834
One, two, three.

00:28:51.709 --> 00:28:53.211
What? What's wrong?

00:28:53.294 --> 00:28:54.420
-What happened?
-Bee! A bee!

00:28:54.504 --> 00:28:56.214
-There's a bee. A bee!
-A bee? Where?

00:28:56.297 --> 00:28:57.340
Where?

00:29:01.135 --> 00:29:03.721
It's not a bee. It's a ladybug.

00:29:03.805 --> 00:29:06.349
What on earth is so terrifying
about this tiny little thing?

00:29:07.058 --> 00:29:08.351
Well…

00:29:08.935 --> 00:29:11.020
I experienced
a traumatic hornet sting in the past.

00:29:15.275 --> 00:29:16.484
Don't laugh.

00:29:16.985 --> 00:29:18.194
I said don't laugh.

00:29:18.987 --> 00:29:22.740
You didn't even bat an eyelash
in front of organ harvesters.

00:29:22.824 --> 00:29:24.868
Childhood scars last a long time.

00:29:24.951 --> 00:29:27.412
That's a childhood scar?

00:29:27.495 --> 00:29:29.789
-Don't make fun of me.
-Right, I'm so sorry.

00:29:29.873 --> 00:29:32.458
-Wait, there's a bee!
-Where?

00:29:35.044 --> 00:29:35.920
Don't laugh.

00:29:38.590 --> 00:29:40.425
Wait, Mr. Gong, it's a real bee this time.

00:29:40.508 --> 00:29:41.926
I'm not lying. Oh no.

00:29:42.010 --> 00:29:43.469
You're going to get stung.

00:29:45.013 --> 00:29:46.222
Stop it!

00:29:46.306 --> 00:29:47.682
-Let's go catch it!
-Stop it!

00:29:48.558 --> 00:29:49.767
I told you to stop.

00:29:55.398 --> 00:29:57.358
It's been a while
since we came here together.

00:29:59.402 --> 00:30:00.862
How's your mother doing?

00:30:02.739 --> 00:30:04.741
She has her ups and downs.

00:30:04.824 --> 00:30:06.326
I hope she gets better soon.

00:30:07.035 --> 00:30:07.994
Recently,

00:30:08.077 --> 00:30:11.539
I've been thinking a lot about the days
when she was the executive director.

00:30:11.623 --> 00:30:13.374
She built this park,

00:30:13.458 --> 00:30:15.710
ran a tree-planting campaign,
and even raised funds

00:30:15.793 --> 00:30:17.170
for environmental protection.

00:30:17.253 --> 00:30:20.131
I took great pride in my work back then.

00:30:20.214 --> 00:30:23.635
It sounds like Mr. Gong's mother
did a lot of good.

00:30:25.553 --> 00:30:27.430
But now, they've all been discontinued,

00:30:27.513 --> 00:30:30.058
and I heard they're planning to
sell this park as well.

00:30:30.141 --> 00:30:31.225
Why?

00:30:32.101 --> 00:30:34.479
Because a company's goal
is to maximize profit.

00:30:34.562 --> 00:30:36.439
Without a clear guiding philosophy
at the helm,

00:30:36.522 --> 00:30:39.108
social responsibility activities
fall to the wayside.

00:30:39.734 --> 00:30:40.818
That's too bad.

00:30:41.569 --> 00:30:43.738
It would've been nice
if they could've actively promoted

00:30:43.821 --> 00:30:46.658
the tree-planting campaign
and this park from the get-go.

00:30:47.241 --> 00:30:48.076
Pardon?

00:30:48.159 --> 00:30:49.953
If it's a similar-quality product,

00:30:50.036 --> 00:30:51.496
moms are bound to favor companies

00:30:52.205 --> 00:30:56.084
that actively engage
in environmental protection efforts.

00:30:57.377 --> 00:30:59.921
Since this is the world
their children will grow up and live in,

00:31:00.004 --> 00:31:01.631
they want to do their part.

00:31:03.758 --> 00:31:05.677
Why does it have the same name as me?

00:31:05.760 --> 00:31:06.594
GONG JI-HYEOK TREE

00:31:06.678 --> 00:31:08.346
Because it was planted for your sake.

00:31:09.764 --> 00:31:14.727
I named it after you, wishing it'd grow
tall and strong alongside you,

00:31:14.811 --> 00:31:16.521
while making the world a cleaner place.

00:31:17.063 --> 00:31:19.107
Because you're bound to be happier

00:31:19.190 --> 00:31:21.067
in a cleaner world.

00:31:21.651 --> 00:31:24.445
Then we should plant a lot of trees.

00:31:25.029 --> 00:31:26.531
So everyone can be happy.

00:31:31.786 --> 00:31:32.996
Ta-da.

00:31:33.079 --> 00:31:34.330
Mom, do you remember?

00:31:35.081 --> 00:31:36.457
That's the tree we planted.

00:31:37.166 --> 00:31:38.251
This is how much it's grown.

00:31:38.835 --> 00:31:39.836
You're right, it has.

00:31:40.461 --> 00:31:41.379
Right?

00:31:41.462 --> 00:31:45.508
I used to live life
with such passion and energy.

00:31:47.385 --> 00:31:48.720
It was all in vain.

00:31:51.055 --> 00:31:53.433
I don't even know
what's left of it anymore.

00:31:58.312 --> 00:31:59.439
Yeah, you do.

00:32:00.481 --> 00:32:01.482
You have me.

00:32:03.901 --> 00:32:07.071
You have your son right here by your side.

00:32:10.158 --> 00:32:11.409
Speaking of which,

00:32:12.076 --> 00:32:13.661
I'm actually trying to turn that dream

00:32:14.620 --> 00:32:15.955
you worked so hard for

00:32:16.998 --> 00:32:18.624
into reality.

00:32:20.126 --> 00:32:21.627
So you need to get well quickly

00:32:22.462 --> 00:32:23.921
and watch me do it.

00:32:24.630 --> 00:32:25.840
Okay?

00:32:43.274 --> 00:32:45.151
Stop moving.

00:32:45.234 --> 00:32:48.029
You're being exceptionally sweet today.

00:32:48.112 --> 00:32:50.573
Well, you've been through a lot.

00:32:51.157 --> 00:32:52.033
What do you mean?

00:32:53.201 --> 00:32:54.660
When you gave birth to me,

00:32:55.328 --> 00:32:56.913
you must've felt so wronged

00:32:58.039 --> 00:32:59.957
getting that surgery
after going through all that pain.

00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:03.086
I'm apologizing for that now.

00:33:03.169 --> 00:33:05.088
Am I finally being rewarded for that now?

00:33:05.171 --> 00:33:07.215
Wow, you really took your time with that.

00:33:08.716 --> 00:33:11.594
I heard the moms talking at work.

00:33:12.428 --> 00:33:15.223
Just hearing about it
sounded so terrifying.

00:33:15.306 --> 00:33:17.600
How did you endure all that pain?

00:33:19.894 --> 00:33:22.730
-When you endure all that pain,
-Yeah?

00:33:22.814 --> 00:33:24.774
you end up with a daughter like this.

00:33:24.857 --> 00:33:25.775
So why wouldn't you?

00:33:27.193 --> 00:33:29.612
I'd gladly give birth to you again
if I had to.

00:33:30.446 --> 00:33:31.489
You're just too cute.

00:33:33.658 --> 00:33:34.492
Go on.

00:33:37.036 --> 00:33:38.704
-Stay still, ma'am.
-Okay.

00:33:39.497 --> 00:33:41.541
-Careful.
-That tickles.

00:33:48.339 --> 00:33:49.173
Just getting home?

00:33:49.882 --> 00:33:50.758
Yeah.

00:33:50.842 --> 00:33:51.884
You're late.

00:33:51.968 --> 00:33:53.594
I went to see my mom.

00:33:53.678 --> 00:33:54.512
What about dinner?

00:33:56.556 --> 00:33:59.100
Hey, do you have ramyeon?

00:33:59.183 --> 00:34:01.352
That looks so good.

00:34:01.435 --> 00:34:02.979
Bon appétit.

00:34:08.359 --> 00:34:09.360
-Is it good?
-Yeah.

00:34:10.069 --> 00:34:12.572
I guess Jun went to bed early.

00:34:12.655 --> 00:34:14.699
Yeah, they apparently had a race
at daycare today.

00:34:14.782 --> 00:34:15.950
He's knocked out.

00:34:16.033 --> 00:34:17.577
He's such a cutie pie.

00:34:19.912 --> 00:34:20.746
It's so spicy.

00:34:23.916 --> 00:34:26.335
How's your mom doing?
I called her earlier.

00:34:27.086 --> 00:34:28.254
The doctor said

00:34:28.337 --> 00:34:31.215
she's recovering quickly
with little to no long-term complications.

00:34:31.299 --> 00:34:32.383
That's a relief.

00:34:35.511 --> 00:34:36.387
Hang in there.

00:34:37.054 --> 00:34:39.640
Seeing her get better
gives me all the energy I need.

00:34:39.724 --> 00:34:41.100
Even work is fun.

00:34:41.184 --> 00:34:43.311
Did your team leader say anything
about the money?

00:34:43.394 --> 00:34:44.729
He just wants the principal.

00:34:46.480 --> 00:34:48.191
You know,

00:34:48.274 --> 00:34:50.610
when he was saving me
from the loan sharks,

00:34:50.693 --> 00:34:53.696
he was super charismatic,
saying things like, "Do you take credit?"

00:34:53.779 --> 00:34:56.574
But it turns out he's terrified of bugs.

00:34:56.657 --> 00:34:58.659
This tiny ladybug made him go frantic,
and he was all,

00:34:59.202 --> 00:35:01.078
"Bee! There's a bee!"

00:35:01.162 --> 00:35:02.830
He was freaking out.

00:35:04.498 --> 00:35:05.833
Isn't that hilarious?

00:35:05.917 --> 00:35:07.168
Was it that funny?

00:35:07.251 --> 00:35:09.337
What? I thought it was.
You don't think so?

00:35:09.921 --> 00:35:11.714
I guess. Sure.

00:35:13.132 --> 00:35:14.133
So funny.

00:35:16.469 --> 00:35:17.762
This quarter,

00:35:17.845 --> 00:35:19.931
we plan to focus on
corporate image marketing.

00:35:20.556 --> 00:35:23.851
We're planning a global marketing campaign
with international celebrities.

00:35:23.935 --> 00:35:25.686
What do you think, Mr. Gong?

00:35:25.770 --> 00:35:26.729
I'm not sure.

00:35:28.648 --> 00:35:31.317
Wouldn't environmental issues
be a better fit for a global campaign?

00:35:31.400 --> 00:35:33.152
-Are you serious?
-Hold on.

00:35:34.278 --> 00:35:36.530
Go on. What exactly do you propose?

00:35:37.114 --> 00:35:39.909
We could revive
our discontinued tree-planting campaign

00:35:39.992 --> 00:35:42.578
to highlight and promote
Natural BeBe's long-standing commitment

00:35:42.662 --> 00:35:46.457
to environmental protection
since its founding.

00:35:46.540 --> 00:35:49.293
It's not a bad idea
for the domestic market.

00:35:49.877 --> 00:35:53.589
But at the brink of global expansion,
we first need a solid corporate image--

00:35:53.673 --> 00:35:56.259
That's what makes it
all the more compelling.

00:35:56.342 --> 00:35:59.262
The global trend is pursuing
environmental protection,

00:35:59.345 --> 00:36:01.514
social responsibility,
and transparent management

00:36:01.597 --> 00:36:02.807
through ESG management.

00:36:02.890 --> 00:36:06.102
Furthermore, ESG indexes
have recently started to be reflected

00:36:06.185 --> 00:36:07.645
in the International Financial
Reporting Standards.

00:36:07.728 --> 00:36:09.313
This indicates that companies

00:36:09.397 --> 00:36:11.691
can now attract global investment
based on their contributions

00:36:12.984 --> 00:36:15.486
to environmental protection
and social responsibility.

00:36:15.569 --> 00:36:18.948
Is there anything more important
than securing funds when it comes to

00:36:20.408 --> 00:36:21.284
business expansion?

00:36:26.872 --> 00:36:28.124
You make a good point.

00:36:28.207 --> 00:36:31.043
I want to see a detailed proposal
from both of you by next week.

00:36:31.127 --> 00:36:32.461
I'll decide after you present.

00:36:36.924 --> 00:36:38.259
A competitive pitch?

00:36:38.843 --> 00:36:40.636
Against the marketing team, at that?

00:36:40.720 --> 00:36:41.762
Yes.

00:36:41.846 --> 00:36:44.265
Shouldn't experts with real experience
handle that?

00:36:44.348 --> 00:36:47.101
You scolded us for being reckless,

00:36:47.184 --> 00:36:48.728
but you're even more reckless than we are.

00:36:48.811 --> 00:36:49.770
Tell me about it.

00:36:49.854 --> 00:36:53.941
We're busy raising kids,
so we don't know anything about trends.

00:36:54.025 --> 00:36:55.276
I believe this project

00:36:56.068 --> 00:36:58.404
should be grounded
in the genuine sentiments of mothers,

00:36:58.487 --> 00:37:00.364
not in fleeting trends.

00:37:00.448 --> 00:37:01.699
That way,

00:37:01.782 --> 00:37:03.326
we'd be able to deliver a clearer

00:37:03.409 --> 00:37:05.411
and more heartfelt message
from a parent's perspective.

00:37:05.995 --> 00:37:09.540
Also, this idea came from our team,
so it's only right that we see it through.

00:37:09.623 --> 00:37:11.417
From our team? Who?

00:37:14.170 --> 00:37:15.254
Ms. Go Da-rim.

00:37:15.713 --> 00:37:17.131
Smarter than appearances suggest.

00:37:19.759 --> 00:37:21.886
-Really?
-When did you think of that?

00:37:21.969 --> 00:37:22.845
I did?

00:37:22.928 --> 00:37:24.847
Your talk with the CSR team leader.

00:37:24.930 --> 00:37:26.349
Oh, that?

00:37:26.432 --> 00:37:27.850
Brief the team on it

00:37:28.684 --> 00:37:30.102
and lead the brainstorming session.

00:37:30.186 --> 00:37:31.896
Yes, sir. I will.

00:37:34.732 --> 00:37:35.649
Let's be sure to win…

00:37:39.653 --> 00:37:40.613
this presentation.

00:37:40.696 --> 00:37:41.697
Okay.

00:37:49.497 --> 00:37:51.749
Thank you for the praise earlier.

00:37:53.751 --> 00:37:56.670
It feels really good to hear
that I helped out the team.

00:37:56.754 --> 00:37:58.506
I praised you?

00:37:58.589 --> 00:38:00.174
You, Ms. Go Da-rim? When?

00:38:00.257 --> 00:38:02.051
You said I was smart.

00:38:02.134 --> 00:38:03.677
I was commenting on a smart brain.

00:38:03.761 --> 00:38:05.805
I never said you were smart.

00:38:06.722 --> 00:38:07.890
It seems you took it the wrong way.

00:38:10.226 --> 00:38:11.560
What I praised

00:38:12.269 --> 00:38:13.938
was this brain here.

00:38:14.021 --> 00:38:15.439
And who does it belong to?

00:38:15.523 --> 00:38:16.607
Me.

00:38:20.736 --> 00:38:23.030
I guess it was self-praise.

00:38:25.616 --> 00:38:26.826
Of course.

00:38:31.914 --> 00:38:33.207
-A photographer?
-Yeah.

00:38:33.290 --> 00:38:34.625
I'm working on an ad concept,

00:38:34.708 --> 00:38:37.294
and I remembered you said you were
preparing for a photography exhibition.

00:38:37.795 --> 00:38:39.255
I thought you might know someone talented.

00:38:39.338 --> 00:38:41.882
It got canceled.
My dad doesn't want me to do it.

00:38:41.966 --> 00:38:43.676
Oh yeah? Well, that's too bad.

00:38:44.844 --> 00:38:45.678
Wait.

00:38:45.761 --> 00:38:47.304
I do know a photographer.

00:38:51.058 --> 00:38:52.017
LEVER DU SOLEIL
KIM SEON-U

00:38:58.691 --> 00:39:00.651
What do you think? Aren't they so nice?

00:39:00.734 --> 00:39:01.610
Yeah.

00:39:02.736 --> 00:39:04.071
It's natural and warm.

00:39:05.448 --> 00:39:06.323
Right?

00:39:06.866 --> 00:39:08.659
He's a warm person.

00:39:08.742 --> 00:39:12.455
He's warm-hearted and speaks warmly too.

00:39:12.538 --> 00:39:13.497
And his face

00:39:14.415 --> 00:39:16.083
is just full of so much warmth.

00:39:16.167 --> 00:39:18.002
I think he'll fit the vibe
we're going for.

00:39:18.085 --> 00:39:19.336
Give me his number.

00:39:19.420 --> 00:39:24.508
I worked my butt off
to uncover this photographer.

00:39:24.592 --> 00:39:28.095
He was completely hidden
like some dinosaur fossil.

00:39:28.179 --> 00:39:29.680
I guess you want something in return.

00:39:29.763 --> 00:39:31.474
Let me in on that project.

00:39:36.896 --> 00:39:39.565
-The pressure's giving me indigestion.
-Me too.

00:39:39.648 --> 00:39:42.485
I'd much rather be weeding.

00:39:42.568 --> 00:39:44.987
I think the big budget
makes it that much worse.

00:39:45.571 --> 00:39:46.697
So much pressure.

00:39:48.073 --> 00:39:50.367
My goodness, look who it is.

00:39:51.076 --> 00:39:53.454
It's our rival team.

00:39:55.080 --> 00:39:57.958
So? Is your presentation
coming along well?

00:39:58.792 --> 00:40:00.628
It's our first ad, so it's a bit daunting.

00:40:00.711 --> 00:40:02.338
-But still--
-Of course, it's daunting.

00:40:02.421 --> 00:40:03.839
Most certainly.

00:40:03.923 --> 00:40:07.051
Advertisement planning is no joke.

00:40:07.134 --> 00:40:09.637
If every Tom, Dick, and Harry could do it,

00:40:09.720 --> 00:40:11.639
then why would our marketing team exist?

00:40:12.348 --> 00:40:13.182
Don't you agree?

00:40:13.265 --> 00:40:14.141
-Yes.
-Of course.

00:40:15.351 --> 00:40:17.061
What's wrong? Are you insulted?

00:40:17.144 --> 00:40:21.106
Your loser team
was just for show from the start!

00:40:22.483 --> 00:40:24.193
You should just focus on

00:40:24.276 --> 00:40:27.613
changing those diapers
and pulling out those weeds at the park.

00:40:27.696 --> 00:40:31.450
How dare you covet
someone else's livelihood?

00:40:32.493 --> 00:40:34.453
"Loser team"?
"Every Tom, Dick, and Harry"?

00:40:34.537 --> 00:40:36.497
-Have you lost your damn mind?
-Calm down, Nan-suk.

00:40:36.580 --> 00:40:38.165
What did you say? Why this lady…

00:40:38.249 --> 00:40:40.918
Do you think we're in a market
where the loudest person wins?

00:40:41.001 --> 00:40:42.545
This is a workplace!

00:40:42.628 --> 00:40:43.921
You should be competing with your skills!

00:40:44.672 --> 00:40:45.714
Yes!

00:40:45.798 --> 00:40:47.258
That's correct!

00:40:52.596 --> 00:40:56.392
That's why we're doing
a competitive pitch, are we not?

00:40:56.475 --> 00:40:57.309
What?

00:40:57.393 --> 00:41:00.145
Forget your title in the hierarchy,
which team you're on,

00:41:00.229 --> 00:41:02.940
and whose inner circle you belong to.

00:41:03.023 --> 00:41:04.817
Is there anything better

00:41:04.900 --> 00:41:07.528
than a competitive pitch
to truly assess skill?

00:41:07.611 --> 00:41:08.487
Right?

00:41:09.113 --> 00:41:11.073
-But that's--
-She's right!

00:41:11.156 --> 00:41:13.450
We're trying to compete with our skills,
so what's the issue?

00:41:13.534 --> 00:41:16.412
Maybe they're scared of losing
their livelihoods to the loser team.

00:41:16.495 --> 00:41:17.788
What? Scared?

00:41:17.871 --> 00:41:19.582
That must be it.

00:41:19.665 --> 00:41:24.378
Why would I be scared of stay-at-home moms
whose only experience is changing diapers?

00:41:25.546 --> 00:41:26.463
You should

00:41:27.172 --> 00:41:28.132
be scared.

00:41:28.716 --> 00:41:30.384
Stay-at-home moms

00:41:30.467 --> 00:41:33.053
are the key demographic
the marketing team should be winning over.

00:41:33.137 --> 00:41:35.973
Now, those very ladies
are getting involved directly.

00:41:36.056 --> 00:41:37.600
-Right?
-Right.

00:41:37.683 --> 00:41:38.601
Right.

00:41:38.684 --> 00:41:41.186
Enjoy the rest of your meal then.

00:41:41.270 --> 00:41:43.147
-Shall we get going now?
-Yes.

00:41:43.230 --> 00:41:45.524
-I'm done eating.
-Yes.

00:41:45.608 --> 00:41:47.067
-Let's go.
-My goodness.

00:41:52.406 --> 00:41:53.407
Why those…

00:41:54.408 --> 00:41:56.910
I ought to just…

00:42:04.335 --> 00:42:06.045
Is the pressure still too much?

00:42:06.128 --> 00:42:07.921
Screw the pressure or whatever.

00:42:08.005 --> 00:42:10.382
I can't contain this anger inside me.

00:42:10.466 --> 00:42:13.010
Do you still want to go weeding
in the park?

00:42:13.093 --> 00:42:14.178
No.

00:42:14.261 --> 00:42:17.348
Forget the weeds.
I want to pull Ma's hair out.

00:42:17.431 --> 00:42:18.557
And you, Go-eun?

00:42:18.641 --> 00:42:20.351
Do you find the big budget intimidating?

00:42:20.434 --> 00:42:22.019
Screw it.

00:42:22.102 --> 00:42:23.812
Sink or swim, we need to go for it.

00:42:26.190 --> 00:42:29.151
You've all heard of
this saying before, right?

00:42:29.735 --> 00:42:32.905
Those who seek death shall live,
and those who seek life shall die.

00:42:34.865 --> 00:42:36.116
Let's go!

00:42:50.714 --> 00:42:51.590
-You're right.
-Something like this.

00:42:52.257 --> 00:42:53.217
I agree.

00:43:41.014 --> 00:43:41.849
Here you go.

00:43:53.152 --> 00:43:54.027
Okay.

00:43:55.904 --> 00:43:57.156
Found it!

00:43:57.239 --> 00:43:58.699
This is it.

00:43:59.658 --> 00:44:02.536
Look at this. Right here.

00:44:02.619 --> 00:44:04.079
AN EYE-CATCHING AD COPY

00:44:04.163 --> 00:44:05.998
SHOW WHY PLANTING TREES BENEFITS OUR KIDS!

00:44:11.628 --> 00:44:15.424
KEYWORDS: TREE, HEALTH, LOVE

00:44:19.094 --> 00:44:21.180
We're done!

00:44:21.263 --> 00:44:22.848
-Finally!
-It looks amazing!

00:44:22.931 --> 00:44:24.349
-You haven't eaten yet, right?
-Oh my gosh!

00:44:38.697 --> 00:44:40.365
A GREEN FUTURE WE DRAW TOGETHER

00:44:40.449 --> 00:44:42.117
GROWING UP MEANS BECOMING STRONGER
WITHOUT ANYONE NOTICING

00:44:52.169 --> 00:44:54.046
We brought tteokbokki and fried sides!

00:44:54.129 --> 00:44:56.131
-Let's eat.
-No, stop!

00:44:56.215 --> 00:44:57.466
-Not here.
-I'll take them over there.

00:44:57.549 --> 00:44:58.467
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:45:04.473 --> 00:45:06.099
Where are the plates again?

00:45:06.183 --> 00:45:07.017
Over here.

00:45:15.734 --> 00:45:16.902
The concept looks good.

00:45:16.985 --> 00:45:17.903
A GREEN FUTURE WE DRAW TOGETHER

00:45:17.986 --> 00:45:19.279
The copies are also excellent.

00:45:19.363 --> 00:45:20.864
The sample shoot
is all we have left now, right?

00:45:21.573 --> 00:45:22.699
Have you contacted the photographer?

00:45:22.783 --> 00:45:24.159
Yes. He agreed to do it.

00:45:24.243 --> 00:45:25.577
I set up a meeting as well.

00:45:25.661 --> 00:45:27.746
Okay. Great.

00:45:28.747 --> 00:45:30.582
What? Where are you going to work?

00:45:30.666 --> 00:45:32.543
Have you lost your mind?

00:45:34.294 --> 00:45:38.048
I mean, the offer was too good
to turn down.

00:45:38.131 --> 00:45:40.509
A big corporate project
would also look good on my resume.

00:45:41.343 --> 00:45:44.972
I mean, who am I to tell you what to do?

00:45:45.055 --> 00:45:47.015
I don't want to
stand in the way of your career.

00:45:47.099 --> 00:45:48.767
But just thinking about it

00:45:48.850 --> 00:45:51.019
is suffocating.

00:45:51.645 --> 00:45:55.315
Maybe my being there
could help you ease up a bit.

00:45:55.899 --> 00:45:58.277
If everyone knows I'm your husband,
it'll clear up all the doubts.

00:45:58.360 --> 00:46:00.404
But that won't be the case, will it?

00:46:00.487 --> 00:46:03.949
I feel like our awkward acting
will just give it all away.

00:46:04.575 --> 00:46:05.742
"Awkward acting"?

00:46:06.785 --> 00:46:08.912
Did you forget I played Romeo
in my high school drama club?

00:46:08.996 --> 00:46:12.416
The competition
was a whopping 12 to 1 back then.

00:46:12.499 --> 00:46:14.084
Don't worry about my acting skills.

00:46:14.167 --> 00:46:17.504
Just look at yourself.
How could I not worry?

00:46:17.588 --> 00:46:19.381
You must've lost your mind!

00:46:19.464 --> 00:46:23.010
You'd better stay on your toes,
or we're both done for.

00:46:23.093 --> 00:46:25.137
-You hear me?
-Don't worry about my acting skills!

00:46:25.721 --> 00:46:27.723
I seriously can't believe you!

00:46:32.060 --> 00:46:32.978
What?

00:46:34.646 --> 00:46:35.522
Hello.

00:46:42.738 --> 00:46:43.739
Hey!

00:46:44.990 --> 00:46:45.991
Hold on.

00:46:46.491 --> 00:46:47.409
What is it?

00:46:47.492 --> 00:46:48.452
Let's just stay here for a bit.

00:46:59.713 --> 00:47:01.131
-The elevator's here. Let's go.
-Hey!

00:47:01.214 --> 00:47:02.257
Please hold the door!

00:47:06.553 --> 00:47:08.972
You could've just dropped her off
at the building entrance.

00:47:09.765 --> 00:47:10.724
She's not a child, you know.

00:47:13.268 --> 00:47:14.645
I'm also on my way to work.

00:47:16.563 --> 00:47:17.439
Here.

00:47:18.357 --> 00:47:20.942
I have a meeting with Mr. Kang Gyeong-min.

00:47:21.026 --> 00:47:22.569
Why would you meet with Mr. Kang?

00:47:23.070 --> 00:47:24.446
I look forward to working with you.

00:47:25.864 --> 00:47:27.157
I'm Kim Seon-u.

00:47:35.540 --> 00:47:37.334
My wife told me what you did.

00:47:37.417 --> 00:47:39.628
I don't know how to thank you.

00:47:40.671 --> 00:47:42.589
We'll pay you back as soon as we can.

00:47:43.382 --> 00:47:44.257
Forget the money.

00:47:44.341 --> 00:47:47.636
Were you aware
of just how much danger she was in?

00:47:49.930 --> 00:47:50.972
She was, wasn't she?

00:47:51.056 --> 00:47:53.392
My wife can be quite stubborn.

00:47:53.475 --> 00:47:55.644
I told her repeatedly
that I'd come pick her up,

00:47:55.727 --> 00:47:58.689
but she stopped me because she didn't know
when she'd be done with work.

00:47:58.772 --> 00:48:01.942
We actually had our first fight
as a married couple because of that.

00:48:03.735 --> 00:48:06.405
-"First"?
-Yes, our first.

00:48:08.615 --> 00:48:11.284
Oh, I see.

00:48:13.036 --> 00:48:14.663
You've never fought before.

00:48:16.289 --> 00:48:18.333
My friend fought with his wife,

00:48:19.167 --> 00:48:21.753
and his wife even ran away to Jeju
for a few days.

00:48:24.506 --> 00:48:26.174
That would never happen with us.

00:48:26.258 --> 00:48:29.845
My Rim can't even sleep
without me by her side.

00:48:37.060 --> 00:48:38.019
Excuse me.

00:48:50.991 --> 00:48:52.868
Where's Mr. Gong Ji-hyeok's office?

00:48:54.244 --> 00:48:56.288
He's in the middle of a meeting right now.

00:48:56.913 --> 00:48:58.790
Do you have an appointment?

00:48:58.874 --> 00:49:00.083
It's fine.

00:49:00.167 --> 00:49:02.419
I don't need to make one to see him.

00:49:08.508 --> 00:49:10.844
Mr. Gong, you have a guest.

00:49:11.511 --> 00:49:12.721
Thanks,

00:49:12.804 --> 00:49:13.972
honey.

00:49:14.765 --> 00:49:16.641
"Honey"?

00:49:23.857 --> 00:49:24.691
Hey, Ha-yeong.

00:49:25.567 --> 00:49:26.651
What brings you here?

00:49:28.528 --> 00:49:30.947
I came by because I heard
you were having your first meeting.

00:49:36.828 --> 00:49:39.372
Deputy Director Yu was the one
who introduced Mr. Kim to me.

00:49:40.582 --> 00:49:41.750
And this is

00:49:42.834 --> 00:49:46.129
a member of my team and Mr. Kim's wife,
Ms. Go Da-rim.

00:49:46.213 --> 00:49:48.882
It's nice to meet you. I'm Go Da-rim.

00:49:50.342 --> 00:49:51.843
You're his wife?

00:49:51.927 --> 00:49:53.553
-His wife?
-Ms. Yu?

00:49:56.431 --> 00:49:59.142
There's a work matter

00:49:59.226 --> 00:50:00.477
I'd like to discuss with you.

00:50:01.520 --> 00:50:03.939
We're going to step out for a quick chat.

00:50:04.523 --> 00:50:06.149
-Sure.
-Let's go.

00:50:06.233 --> 00:50:07.776
Come with me.

00:50:07.859 --> 00:50:08.860
Please excuse us.

00:50:08.944 --> 00:50:10.028
Let's go.

00:50:15.116 --> 00:50:17.911
I mean, still,
how could you pretend to be married?

00:50:18.995 --> 00:50:20.205
Wait.

00:50:20.288 --> 00:50:21.122
Just hold on.

00:50:22.082 --> 00:50:25.418
Her mother practically saved my life.

00:50:26.628 --> 00:50:29.214
I knew it was wrong, but I had to help.

00:50:29.923 --> 00:50:33.969
Could you keep this a secret?

00:50:34.052 --> 00:50:35.011
Please.

00:50:35.595 --> 00:50:39.641
So you're saying
this is for her mother's sake

00:50:39.724 --> 00:50:41.268
and not for her sake, right?

00:50:43.478 --> 00:50:44.396
Right.

00:50:44.479 --> 00:50:48.608
Then that means you two are definitely,
certainly, positively, absolutely

00:50:49.150 --> 00:50:50.402
just friends, right?

00:50:51.778 --> 00:50:52.863
Yes.

00:50:59.786 --> 00:51:01.454
That's quite an unfortunate situation,

00:51:01.538 --> 00:51:05.458
but my conscience will simply not allow me
to overlook a crime.

00:51:08.128 --> 00:51:11.339
However, I could turn a blind eye
depending on how you do.

00:51:11.923 --> 00:51:13.300
What do I need to do?

00:51:13.383 --> 00:51:15.343
I'll do anything. Just say the word.

00:51:23.727 --> 00:51:25.604
If it makes you uncomfortable,

00:51:25.687 --> 00:51:27.939
I could tell my husband to quit.

00:51:29.524 --> 00:51:30.358
I'm fine.

00:51:31.359 --> 00:51:33.486
If anyone is uncomfortable, it'd be you.

00:51:34.362 --> 00:51:37.490
Unlike someone, I don't have a partner,
nor have I done anything wrong.

00:51:38.158 --> 00:51:39.659
I'm very relaxed.

00:51:40.952 --> 00:51:44.039
You must be worried
I'll snitch to your husband.

00:51:44.789 --> 00:51:45.832
But don't worry.

00:51:47.042 --> 00:51:49.252
Meddling in my team members'
personal affairs…

00:51:51.671 --> 00:51:52.756
is not my cup of tea.

00:51:53.423 --> 00:51:56.718
I didn't mean it like that,

00:51:56.801 --> 00:51:58.553
but thank you anyway.

00:51:58.637 --> 00:52:01.181
If I say I'll forget it, I forget it.

00:52:02.349 --> 00:52:03.850
A mistake.

00:52:03.934 --> 00:52:05.143
A sort of accident.

00:52:05.226 --> 00:52:08.313
A game of ping-pong with a stranger.

00:52:09.689 --> 00:52:11.441
I don't even remember such things.

00:52:11.524 --> 00:52:12.734
I see.

00:52:14.903 --> 00:52:16.780
He remembers every single thing.

00:52:20.825 --> 00:52:22.577
What a small world we live in.

00:52:22.661 --> 00:52:25.205
Who knew you'd be Ms. Go's husband?

00:52:25.288 --> 00:52:27.207
You two make such a great couple.

00:52:27.290 --> 00:52:30.126
-The perfect-looking couple.
-My thoughts exactly.

00:52:30.210 --> 00:52:32.629
And you two sort of resemble one another.

00:52:32.712 --> 00:52:36.007
We've been friends since we were kids.

00:52:36.091 --> 00:52:38.259
I guess we've grown
to resemble one another

00:52:38.343 --> 00:52:39.928
after all those long years.

00:52:40.845 --> 00:52:43.181
How did you go
from being childhood friends

00:52:43.264 --> 00:52:46.434
to lovers, and then, partners?

00:52:47.018 --> 00:52:49.896
Well, you see, what happened was…

00:52:49.980 --> 00:52:51.106
It was just--

00:52:51.189 --> 00:52:54.192
I didn't know at first
because we were longtime friends,

00:52:54.275 --> 00:52:57.112
but I eventually realized
that I had fallen for her.

00:52:58.071 --> 00:52:59.072
And I had fallen for her hard.

00:52:59.990 --> 00:53:01.324
It was one-sided for a while,

00:53:01.408 --> 00:53:04.035
but when I saw her with someone else,
I couldn't stand it anymore.

00:53:04.869 --> 00:53:06.037
So I confessed.

00:53:07.706 --> 00:53:09.541
Why am I getting butterflies?

00:53:09.624 --> 00:53:11.376
Are you sure you've been married
for seven years?

00:53:13.503 --> 00:53:14.838
Sorry about that.

00:53:15.672 --> 00:53:16.589
-What was that for?
-You just flew.

00:53:16.673 --> 00:53:17.716
That's enough chit-chat.

00:53:18.800 --> 00:53:20.593
This is Deputy Director Yu Ha-yeong
from Taeyu Art Hall.

00:53:20.677 --> 00:53:21.970
She'll be organizing
a photography exhibition

00:53:22.053 --> 00:53:23.513
in association with this campaign.

00:53:23.596 --> 00:53:24.889
Hello.

00:53:24.973 --> 00:53:27.267
We've decided to take part
because we liked the campaign's objective.

00:53:27.350 --> 00:53:31.271
We especially plan to support Mr. Kim
as much as we can,

00:53:31.354 --> 00:53:33.648
so please let me know
if you ever need anything.

00:53:33.732 --> 00:53:35.900
Then could you provide support

00:53:35.984 --> 00:53:38.069
for the ad concept shoot
for the presentation?

00:53:38.153 --> 00:53:42.032
We might need to go on a business trip
for some on-site shooting.

00:53:42.115 --> 00:53:42.991
Of course.

00:53:43.074 --> 00:53:46.369
We'll cover all expenses,
wherever it may be.

00:53:47.162 --> 00:53:49.372
We'll even cover an overnight trip.

00:53:50.248 --> 00:53:51.082
Applause.

00:53:57.338 --> 00:53:58.173
-Hey.
-Yeah?

00:53:58.256 --> 00:54:00.216
You're a pretty good actor.

00:54:00.300 --> 00:54:01.843
I almost thought you really liked me.

00:54:01.926 --> 00:54:03.136
Did you?

00:54:03.219 --> 00:54:05.930
How did you come up
with such a love story on the spot?

00:54:06.765 --> 00:54:08.558
Oh, Romeo!

00:54:09.809 --> 00:54:11.352
Do you feel more relaxed now?

00:54:11.436 --> 00:54:12.729
Yeah.

00:54:12.812 --> 00:54:14.230
Thanks, my friend.

00:54:19.069 --> 00:54:21.863
Babe, I'll see you at home later.

00:54:21.946 --> 00:54:23.239
-Okay.
-Ms. Go Da-rim.

00:54:23.323 --> 00:54:24.783
You don't have to do that in front--

00:54:24.866 --> 00:54:25.909
The elevator!

00:54:27.827 --> 00:54:30.121
It's here.

00:54:32.749 --> 00:54:33.833
SHH, IT'S A SECRET!

00:54:33.917 --> 00:54:36.252
-Why did you cut me off?
-Well…

00:54:36.878 --> 00:54:37.879
Ms. Yu.

00:54:37.962 --> 00:54:40.215
Since you said you'd keep it a secret,

00:54:40.298 --> 00:54:43.218
can you just pretend you don't know
in front of Da-rim as well?

00:54:43.301 --> 00:54:45.887
Why? You don't need to act in front of me.

00:54:45.970 --> 00:54:49.516
She may not look it,
but she's really soft-hearted and timid.

00:54:50.600 --> 00:54:52.060
If she knows you know,

00:54:52.143 --> 00:54:54.270
it'll only make her nervous
and get her to mess up.

00:54:55.313 --> 00:54:59.651
So I'd appreciate it
if we could just keep it between us.

00:54:59.734 --> 00:55:01.903
How incredibly considerate of you.

00:55:06.074 --> 00:55:08.368
-Then make time for me today.
-Today?

00:55:09.911 --> 00:55:12.038
I thought of something I want to do.

00:55:13.289 --> 00:55:14.499
Take my first birthday photos.

00:55:16.126 --> 00:55:17.544
Fill this out for me.

00:55:18.253 --> 00:55:19.170
What's this?

00:55:19.254 --> 00:55:22.882
You just have to write down things
that make you smile.

00:55:22.966 --> 00:55:24.676
Things that make me smile?

00:55:31.474 --> 00:55:33.393
FIDE, BABIES, HORSEBACK RIDING,
ACOUSTIC GUITAR,

00:55:33.476 --> 00:55:35.895
BEETHOVEN, QUOKKAS, A KIND AND WARM PERSON

00:55:38.106 --> 00:55:39.399
All right.

00:55:44.112 --> 00:55:46.197
Should we have a little chat?

00:55:46.698 --> 00:55:47.657
How's my pose?

00:55:47.740 --> 00:55:48.867
First time riding one?

00:55:49.534 --> 00:55:51.703
I've been riding horses since I was 6.

00:55:51.786 --> 00:55:53.037
How did it feel

00:55:54.038 --> 00:55:55.039
when you first rode one?

00:55:55.790 --> 00:55:56.875
It was really fun.

00:55:56.958 --> 00:55:59.419
I was really good at connecting
with my horse.

00:55:59.502 --> 00:56:02.463
My horse is so cute. I miss it.

00:56:02.547 --> 00:56:03.506
Where is it now?

00:56:03.590 --> 00:56:05.133
In Jeju Island.

00:56:05.925 --> 00:56:08.428
They're all so cute. I miss them so much.

00:56:58.061 --> 00:56:59.229
Why did you want
a first birthday photoshoot?

00:56:59.312 --> 00:57:00.730
Don't you already have photos from then?

00:57:00.813 --> 00:57:03.650
I don't. My parents were always busy.

00:57:04.192 --> 00:57:06.694
When I was little,
I was almost always alone.

00:57:06.778 --> 00:57:07.820
Well, the housekeeper was there.

00:57:08.404 --> 00:57:10.657
That's why I thought
I should at least take them now.

00:57:10.740 --> 00:57:13.576
They're all pretty similar.
I don't know what to choose.

00:57:18.289 --> 00:57:19.457
Can I see that for a second?

00:57:21.834 --> 00:57:22.794
I think…

00:57:24.420 --> 00:57:27.048
this one, this one,

00:57:27.632 --> 00:57:29.634
and this one are the best.

00:57:31.928 --> 00:57:33.388
Oh, really?

00:57:34.013 --> 00:57:34.931
You think so?

00:57:35.598 --> 00:57:36.766
Yes, they're pretty.

00:57:42.230 --> 00:57:43.523
Why?

00:57:43.606 --> 00:57:46.067
Why are they pretty?

00:57:46.818 --> 00:57:47.944
You're smiling.

00:57:51.281 --> 00:57:52.907
You really look like a baby

00:57:53.491 --> 00:57:54.617
when you smile big like that.

00:57:55.743 --> 00:57:58.288
Since this is
my first birthday photoshoot,

00:57:58.371 --> 00:58:00.540
I'll go with the ones
where I look like a baby.

00:58:00.623 --> 00:58:01.708
Okay.

00:58:01.791 --> 00:58:04.877
Then, this one, this one, and this one.

00:58:04.961 --> 00:58:07.213
I'll print those three for you.

00:58:08.339 --> 00:58:09.382
We're done, right?

00:58:09.882 --> 00:58:11.259
No, not yet.

00:58:11.342 --> 00:58:13.636
I want to make an album.

00:58:13.720 --> 00:58:14.721
The one that carries 22 photos.

00:58:18.308 --> 00:58:20.476
I have a reservation coming up.

00:58:20.560 --> 00:58:21.811
I'm not taking them all today.

00:58:22.395 --> 00:58:24.939
I'll decide the time, location,
and concept.

00:58:25.023 --> 00:58:27.191
You just need to show up
and take the pictures.

00:58:28.026 --> 00:58:30.737
That means we have 19 more to go.

00:58:31.696 --> 00:58:32.822
You already know, right?

00:58:32.905 --> 00:58:34.949
-Guys, hold on.
-If you all have kids, you already know.

00:58:35.033 --> 00:58:36.868
-Of course.
-Big movements.

00:58:36.951 --> 00:58:38.494
-Movements need to be big.
-Yes, that's right.

00:58:38.578 --> 00:58:40.455
We're going with an eco-friendly concept.

00:58:40.538 --> 00:58:42.290
-Yes, that's what we're going for.
-That's right.

00:58:48.796 --> 00:58:50.673
Come this way!

00:58:51.966 --> 00:58:54.969
Amazing! Keep going!

00:58:55.053 --> 00:58:56.387
That's it!

00:59:00.808 --> 00:59:02.769
Keep going!

00:59:03.645 --> 00:59:05.480
Who wants to follow these?

00:59:05.563 --> 00:59:07.148
Who wants to follow me?

00:59:07.231 --> 00:59:09.525
Who wants to catch them?

00:59:15.948 --> 00:59:17.742
Let's take a short break.

00:59:17.825 --> 00:59:19.202
-Okay.
-Let's take a break, kids.

00:59:19.285 --> 00:59:21.621
Let's go and take a break.

00:59:21.704 --> 00:59:22.747
Kids.

00:59:25.833 --> 00:59:26.834
Kim Seon-u.

00:59:28.211 --> 00:59:30.171
-That's great.
-Don't take my picture.

00:59:30.254 --> 00:59:31.214
It's nice. Keep going.

00:59:33.049 --> 00:59:33.883
Take a look.

00:59:35.051 --> 00:59:36.678
-What is that?
-It came out well.

00:59:37.637 --> 00:59:40.181
You're pretty cool today. A total pro.

00:59:40.264 --> 00:59:43.184
That's nothing new.
You've seen me work before.

00:59:43.267 --> 00:59:45.895
But still, it's definitely different
seeing you outside of the studio.

00:59:45.978 --> 00:59:46.979
-Hold on.
-What?

00:59:47.063 --> 00:59:49.148
You have something here.

00:59:49.691 --> 00:59:50.608
Thanks.

00:59:51.109 --> 00:59:52.985
Then take a pretty shot of me.

00:59:54.862 --> 00:59:55.780
Try jumping.

00:59:55.863 --> 00:59:56.989
That's good.

00:59:57.073 --> 00:59:58.616
Have some more fun.

00:59:58.700 --> 00:59:59.909
Oh, me?

01:00:01.661 --> 01:00:04.414
-You call that just being friends?
-Hold on.

01:00:04.497 --> 01:00:07.083
Mr. Kim, let's eat before we continue.

01:00:09.460 --> 01:00:10.795
The air is no good here.

01:00:10.878 --> 01:00:11.754
Let's go.

01:00:13.798 --> 01:00:16.676
-Mother!
-TF!

01:00:16.759 --> 01:00:17.635
Good job today.

01:00:17.719 --> 01:00:19.429
-Good work today.
-Well done.

01:00:19.512 --> 01:00:21.806
-That's refreshing.
-My goodness, that's good.

01:00:21.889 --> 01:00:24.684
It's been forever
since I've had such a feast.

01:00:24.767 --> 01:00:26.102
It feels like it's my birthday.

01:00:26.185 --> 01:00:27.186
It'll be my treat today,

01:00:27.270 --> 01:00:29.355
-so please enjoy to your heart's content.
-Will do.

01:00:29.439 --> 01:00:30.857
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

01:00:30.940 --> 01:00:34.110
It's been years since I've eaten out
without having to look after the kids.

01:00:34.193 --> 01:00:37.321
What do you say
to just one business trip every week?

01:00:37.405 --> 01:00:38.406
Should we?

01:00:40.825 --> 01:00:42.243
-Da-rim, there's no meat there.
-Yeah?

01:00:42.326 --> 01:00:44.078
-Nan-suk, this is so tasty.
-Is it?

01:00:45.538 --> 01:00:47.206
-Abalones.
-Thank you.

01:00:48.124 --> 01:00:48.958
Thank you.

01:00:53.755 --> 01:00:55.465
Mr. Kim, you should eat too.

01:00:55.548 --> 01:00:58.342
You worked the hardest today,
but you're only taking care of your wife.

01:00:58.426 --> 01:01:00.052
Sorry, it's just become a habit.

01:01:01.804 --> 01:01:02.805
Eat up, honey.

01:01:03.931 --> 01:01:05.057
Honey…

01:01:11.731 --> 01:01:12.899
You too, honey.

01:01:14.108 --> 01:01:17.445
They're just overflowing with love.
I saw it earlier during the shoot too.

01:01:17.528 --> 01:01:19.572
Where can you even find
a husband like that?

01:01:19.655 --> 01:01:21.824
When a husband treats his wife
as well as he does,

01:01:21.908 --> 01:01:24.076
it's for one of two reasons.

01:01:24.160 --> 01:01:26.704
Number one, he's not human. He's an angel.

01:01:26.788 --> 01:01:30.458
Or number two, he has a huge secret
he's hiding from his wife.

01:01:37.840 --> 01:01:40.384
What could he be hiding?
It's not like he's cheating on her.

01:01:40.468 --> 01:01:41.594
Of course.

01:01:41.677 --> 01:01:44.514
He's totally an angel. That's it.

01:01:44.597 --> 01:01:47.433
-I'm an angel?
-Of course.

01:01:48.810 --> 01:01:50.394
That's not true.

01:01:51.145 --> 01:01:52.146
The real angel

01:01:52.897 --> 01:01:54.982
is right here.

01:01:56.150 --> 01:01:58.945
-Forget it. Let's just drink.
-Drink up.

01:01:59.028 --> 01:02:01.239
-What did I just see? Jeez.
-Unbelievable.

01:02:01.322 --> 01:02:03.366
Drink up, Nan-suk.

01:02:03.866 --> 01:02:04.784
Jeez.

01:02:15.002 --> 01:02:16.003
How pretty.

01:02:17.713 --> 01:02:20.967
This is the perfect weather
for a first birthday photoshoot.

01:02:21.050 --> 01:02:22.635
Ms. Yu?

01:02:23.553 --> 01:02:26.222
I thought this floral background
would be perfect.

01:02:26.305 --> 01:02:27.598
Right now?

01:02:27.682 --> 01:02:30.393
Yes, I decide the time,
location, and concept.

01:02:30.476 --> 01:02:33.187
And you take the pictures, no matter what.
That was our agreement, no?

01:02:33.771 --> 01:02:34.939
That's right.

01:02:51.372 --> 01:02:52.582
I'm getting tipsy.

01:02:54.208 --> 01:02:55.751
I need some fresh air.

01:02:56.627 --> 01:02:58.880
Da-rim, where are you going?

01:02:58.963 --> 01:03:00.172
I just need some fresh air.

01:03:00.256 --> 01:03:01.841
Have a drink with me when you come back.

01:03:01.924 --> 01:03:04.552
-Okay.
-You drank too much, huh?

01:03:05.386 --> 01:03:06.929
Is Da-rim a lightweight?

01:03:07.013 --> 01:03:08.514
I don't think so.

01:03:09.307 --> 01:03:10.975
Look at her pretending!

01:03:15.479 --> 01:03:17.899
Goodness, Mr. Gong!

01:03:17.982 --> 01:03:20.234
I must pour you a drink.

01:03:20.318 --> 01:03:22.111
I need to have a heart-to-heart with you.

01:03:23.779 --> 01:03:24.947
Bottoms up.

01:03:25.031 --> 01:03:26.198
What a man.

01:03:27.199 --> 01:03:29.619
You need to pour me one too, Mr. Gong.

01:03:29.702 --> 01:03:31.078
Thank you.

01:03:31.162 --> 01:03:32.955
-Gosh, it looks so tasty.
-Me too!

01:03:33.039 --> 01:03:34.624
-Me too.
-Me too.

01:03:34.707 --> 01:03:36.125
I really need to use the bathroom.

01:03:38.210 --> 01:03:39.211
Good.

01:03:39.295 --> 01:03:40.254
That's good.

01:03:42.840 --> 01:03:45.176
-How are they?
-Just a moment.

01:03:47.094 --> 01:03:49.263
They're coming out a bit dark.

01:03:49.347 --> 01:03:50.973
Let's do it next time
with better lighting.

01:03:52.308 --> 01:03:53.476
Okay.

01:03:53.559 --> 01:03:54.685
Let's go.

01:03:55.269 --> 01:03:58.272
You'll need to share a room
with Ms. Go tonight.

01:03:58.356 --> 01:03:59.315
Will you be okay?

01:03:59.398 --> 01:04:02.318
Yes, I'll be fine.
We've been friends for over 20 years.

01:04:03.027 --> 01:04:04.445
That's why it's unsafe…

01:04:04.528 --> 01:04:06.739
I mean, more uncomfortable.

01:04:07.990 --> 01:04:10.284
How about you come out later?

01:04:10.368 --> 01:04:11.577
I'll get you another room.

01:04:11.661 --> 01:04:13.996
-You don't have to do--
-I don't like it.

01:04:21.462 --> 01:04:22.755
Where is she?

01:04:24.006 --> 01:04:24.840
Jeez.

01:04:28.052 --> 01:04:29.637
What's going on? Are they fighting?

01:04:47.321 --> 01:04:49.490
Here you are, Mr. Gong.

01:05:02.503 --> 01:05:04.714
Oh, you must've also needed some fresh--

01:05:41.709 --> 01:05:46.630
DYNAMITE KISS

01:06:16.744 --> 01:06:19.163
What's with you? You look like someone
who desperately needs the bathroom.

01:06:19.246 --> 01:06:20.664
Did you two come together?

01:06:21.832 --> 01:06:23.000
You sure about this?

01:06:23.084 --> 01:06:24.460
-It makes it thrilling.
-Naughty boy.

01:06:24.543 --> 01:06:26.337
They both must've lost their minds.

01:06:26.420 --> 01:06:28.798
What do you think of me as a man?

01:06:28.881 --> 01:06:30.800
Ji-hyeok, I have a crush on someone.

01:06:30.883 --> 01:06:32.843
I saw you and Kim Seon-u kissing.

01:06:33.719 --> 01:06:34.762
This is driving me crazy.

01:06:34.845 --> 01:06:37.807
Ms. Go is just an ordinary woman
and mother.

01:06:37.890 --> 01:06:39.600
Why are you even worried about her?

01:06:40.601 --> 01:06:41.811
Because she's my team member.

01:06:41.894 --> 01:06:46.023
Subtitle translation by: Justin Kim